        title: `3. MANDATORY BIS HALLMARKING COMPLIANCE`,
        rawTitle: `MANDATORY BIS HALLMARKING COMPLIANCE`,
        contentHtml: `<p>3.1   With effect from 1 April 2023, the sale of gold jewellery of 14-karat (585), 18-karat (750), and 22-karat (916) purity without mandatory BIS hallmarking is prohibited for licensed jewellers across all districts of India. aurajewels.commplies with this mandatory hallmarking requirement.</p><p>3.2   All gold jewellery sold by Aura Jewels through the Website is BIS hallmarked in compliance with the mandatory hallmarking orders. Each hallmarked article carries the complete 4-component BIS hallmark as described in Clause 4 of this Policy.</p><p>3.3   Aura Jewels does not sell gold jewellery without a BIS hallmark where hallmarking is legally mandated. Any product listed on the Website as containing gold will be hallmarked as required by law.</p><table><tr><td><p><strong>CONSUMER PROTECTION THROUGH MANDATORY HALLMARKING</strong></p><p>BIS hallmarking with HUID is India's most important consumer protection mechanism for gold jewellery. It independently verifies the purity of the gold and creates a permanent, traceable record of each article. Before purchasing gold jewellery — from any seller — consumers are advised to verify the BIS hallmark and HUID on the article and to independently verify the HUID through the BIS portal at bis.gov.in.</p></td></tr></table>`
