        contentHtml: `<p>4.1   Every BIS hallmarked gold jewellery article carries four distinct marks. All four must be present for the hallmark to be valid:</p><table><tr><td><p><strong>#</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Mark</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Appearance</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>What It Means</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>1</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>BIS Logo</strong></p></td><td><p><em>The BIS triangular logo (India Standards Mark)</em></p></td><td><p>Confirms that the article has been certified by BIS and that the jeweller is a licensed BIS registrant.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>2</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Fineness / Purity Mark</strong></p></td><td><p><em>916 (22K), 750 (18K), 585 (14K) — stamped numerically</em></p></td><td><p>Confirms the gold purity of the article. 916 = 91.6% pure gold (22K). 750 = 75.0% pure gold (18K). 585 = 58.5% pure gold (14K).</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>3</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>AHC Mark</strong></p></td><td><p><em>Unique alphanumeric code of the Assaying &amp; Hallmarking Centre</em></p></td><td><p>Identifies the specific BIS-licensed AHC that tested and hallmarked the article. Enables traceability to the assaying centre.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>4</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>HUID</strong></p></td><td><p><em>6-character alphanumeric code (e.g., AB1234)</em></p></td><td><p>Hallmark Unique Identification — a unique identifier for this specific article. Verifiable online at bis.gov.in. Links the physical article to BIS records.</p></td></tr></table>`
