        contentHtml: `<p>1.1   Cookies are small text files placed on your device (computer, tablet, or mobile) when you visit a website. They allow the website to recognize your device on subsequent visits, remember your preferences, and collect information about how you use the website.</p><p>1.2   In addition to cookies, Aura Jewels's Website uses the following similar technologies:</p><table><tr><td><p><strong>Technology</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Description</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Pixels (Web Beacons)</strong></p></td><td><p>Tiny invisible images embedded in web pages or emails that allow third parties (such as Meta and Google) to detect when a page has been visited or an email opened, and to record the IP address of the device.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Local Storage</strong></p></td><td><p>Similar to cookies but stored in the browser's local storage. Used to retain session preferences and cart contents between pages.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Session Storage</strong></p></td><td><p>Temporary storage that exists only for the duration of a single browser session and is deleted when the browser tab is closed.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Tracking Scripts</strong></p></td><td><p>JavaScript code embedded in Website pages that records user interactions such as clicks, scrolls, navigation paths, and session duration for analytics and advertising purposes.</p></td></tr></table>`
